    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Problem:**\nWhen running `frai gate init --ci` through the CLI, the `--ci` flag was not being passed to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI, so the workflow file wasn't being created. This happened because in Commander.js v11, subcommands don't automatically inherit parent options.\n\n**The Solution:**\nModified the `gate` command handler in `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n\n1. Access both the parent command's options (`command.parent?.opts()`) and the subcommand's options (`command.opts()`)\n2. Merge both option objects together\n3. Reconstruct CLI flags from the merged options (excluding frai-specific options like `--scan`, `--setup`, etc.)\n4. Pass the reconstructed arguments to the `frai-gate` CLI\n\n**Verification:**\n\u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` (the spec template)\n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` (the GitHub Actions workflow)\n\nThe workflow file contains the proper GitHub Actions configuration for running the RAI Gate checks on every PR.",
